  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Selgantolimod and DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase, mediated through the enzyme Magnesium levulinate. Selgantolimod is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Keratin, type II cytoskeletal 6A, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein, all of which are targets of Magnesium levulinate. This indicates that Selgantolimod may interact with these proteins, which in turn interact with DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological pathway. The mechanism likely involves Selgantolimod acting as a modulator of the downstream targets, possibly through enzyme inhibition or regulation. The evidence supports a possible role for Selgantolimod in influencing the activity of DNA-3-methyladenine glycosylase, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
